  "findings": [
    "All12 Vietnam inbound credit rules still cite old procedural pages; current Circular89 Article34 must replace procedure references after source registration.",
    "Current boolean credit effect does not encode tax-sparing or deemed-percentage credits.",
    "Singapore24(2)(b) and24(4), Thailand23(2)(b), Malaysia24(3)/(6), Indonesia23(3)/(4) and India24(3) require separate relief-condition review.",
    "Korea23(3)-(5) describe relief in Korea on Vietnamese income; they must not be reversed into Vietnam relief for Korean income.",
    "Hong Kong22(3) and Singapore24(2)(a) include10-percent direct/indirect ownership requirements for corporate underlying credit."
  ],
